<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0001>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/1%231> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:appliesTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> ;
    rdfs:comment "Modality recorded as `must` on the reading that \"mandatory\" is obligation. The sentence contains no modal verb at all, so nothing in the grammar supports the reading — it is entirely a legal judgement."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0001" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:b6690f96b0ebc5181ac9b42c2669b0de831371538a8cc414e94d5e54796ceeff" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 434 ;
    tmk:spanStart 359 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The application of section 43 is, by the wording of the section, mandatory."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0002>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/1%231> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0051> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:constrainsExaminerTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> ;
    rdfs:comment "Tier 3: a wrong reading here either removes a discretion that exists or preserves one that does not."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0002" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:b6690f96b0ebc5181ac9b42c2669b0de831371538a8cc414e94d5e54796ceeff" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 542 ;
    tmk:spanStart 435 ;
    tmk:supportingText "There is, therefore, no discretion to accept a trade mark that is caught by the provisions of this section."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0003>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/1%231> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0002> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0003" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:b6690f96b0ebc5181ac9b42c2669b0de831371538a8cc414e94d5e54796ceeff" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 777 ;
    tmk:spanStart 543 ;
    tmk:supportingText "However for a trade mark to be caught by these provisions it is necessary for a decision maker to be clearly satisfied that use of the trade mark for the specified goods and / or services would be likely to deceive or cause confusion."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0005>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/3> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:excludesBasis ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdfs:comment "The object is arguably wrong: the excluded basis is the *comparison*, not section 44 — section 44 is where the comparison belongs. GR-0006 records that half. If the two should be one record, say so."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0005" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:f77c8cbb077e1682c601fc3ba31e570dd8097297d2a240565a044a3135e70190" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 106 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A connotation must arise from the trade mark itself, and not through a comparison with another trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0006>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/3> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:allocatesTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Modality left null on purpose. The sentence states where something is dealt with; it directs nobody to do anything, and inventing a modality for it would be exactly the guess the schema forbids."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0006" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:f77c8cbb077e1682c601fc3ba31e570dd8097297d2a240565a044a3135e70190" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 236 ;
    tmk:spanStart 107 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Such comparisons are dealt with under the provisions of section 44 of the Act, and discussed in detail in Part 26 of this Manual."@en ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0007>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0038> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdfs:comment "Recording `may` here and `may` on GR-0034 flattens two different things into one value. If the modality vocabulary needs a fourth value for possibility, this record is the argument for it."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0007" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:1379f8631cf727764dfdb50bbaf252431c91e4e73945cafb375b69e38113fce7" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 84 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A connotation may result from the whole trade mark or from a part of the trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0008>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0050> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdfs:comment "`requiresElement` is probably the wrong predicate — the sentence lists sufficient sources, not necessary elements. Left in deliberately as an example of a predicate that reads plausibly and says the wrong thing."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0008" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:1379f8631cf727764dfdb50bbaf252431c91e4e73945cafb375b69e38113fce7" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 213 ;
    tmk:spanStart 85 ;
    tmk:supportingText "It may result from a dictionary meaning or from a connection in the minds of the buying public with some person, place or thing."@en ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0010>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/4> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(3)> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdfs:comment "Subject and object may be the wrong way round: it is s 33(3) that requires the ground, not the ground that requires s 33(3). Direction is a common and invisible error in relationship extraction."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0010" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:5a52a4dd52ef95b0e001380666cfbc14b907dda998e67a97a99859e9c179e298" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 185 ;
    tmk:spanStart 57 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The Registrar must be satisfied that a ground for rejection exists before section 33(3) can be applied to reject the trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0011>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/2/2/4> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:constrainsExaminerTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0007> ;
    rdfs:comment "A negative \"should\". Whether a negative should is weaker, stronger or the same as a positive one is a reading, and the modality vocabulary cannot express the difference."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0011" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Should ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:5a52a4dd52ef95b0e001380666cfbc14b907dda998e67a97a99859e9c179e298" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 282 ;
    tmk:spanStart 186 ;
    tmk:supportingText "If there is doubt that a connotation exists, then the ground for rejection should not be raised."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0012>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3/3/3> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:interprets ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/CASE/2000/FCA/720> ;
    rdfs:comment "The supporting text is the Manual's proposition, not the Court's words. The Court is cited in the next sentence. If a relationship's supporting text must be the sentence naming the case, this record is wrong and the rule should be stated."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0012" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:4a55810237a8dcf24587418ccacf418cc126ea299e516b2e35e8270f21d56352" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 178 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "At least at the examination stage, deception and confusion must result from something within the trade mark under consideration, not through a comparison with another trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0013>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3%231~1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:citesAuthorityFor ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/CASE/2006/FCA/1663> ;
    rdfs:comment "Direction again: the Manual cites the case, so `citesAuthorityFor` with the case as subject may be backwards."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0013" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:deb607cbc7ae6fd37a648887567b1d4002a2af161e5ab51e486bee19095a59a0" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 288 ;
    tmk:spanStart 49 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The underlying purpose of section 43 is to prevent the public being deceived or confused as to the nature of the goods by reason of the secondary meaning connoted by the mark in question (Pfizer Products Inc v Karam [2006] FCA 1663, [53])."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0014>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3%231~1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43> ;
    rdfs:comment "This is a candidate `authority_conflation` if reproduced as the statutory test — see PU-0004. The Manual's formulation and the Act's differ and both appear within one chunk."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0014" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:deb607cbc7ae6fd37a648887567b1d4002a2af161e5ab51e486bee19095a59a0" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 890 ;
    tmk:spanStart 690 ;
    tmk:supportingText "For a trade mark to trigger section 43 there must be some connotation within the trade mark that would reasonably be expected to cause deception or confusion in the mind of the relevant buying public."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0015>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3%231~1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:doesNotGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0047> ;
    rdfs:comment "Four subjects in one sentence — a person's name, a descriptive term, a place name, a size or use reference. Recording it as one relationship loses three of them; recording it as four repeats the sentence four times. Which is right is a modelling decision."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0015" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:deb607cbc7ae6fd37a648887567b1d4002a2af161e5ab51e486bee19095a59a0" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1541 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1278 ;
    tmk:supportingText "However, the mere presence within a trade mark of a person's name, a descriptive term, a geographical place name or a reference to the size of packages or intended use of a product does not automatically demonstrate a connotation sufficient to trigger section 43."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0016>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3%231~2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdfs:comment "Each of the three adjectives gets its own sub-section in Part 29.3. Whether they are three requirements or one composite standard is worth stating."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0016" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:e910adb71eb7f1d52d06e37ed7b46dc618fcc4f6c6df770466fce554ec158e85" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1214 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1086 ;
    tmk:supportingText "For a ground for rejection to be raised the connotation must be obvious, direct, and immediate and within the trade mark itself."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0017>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3%231~2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0002> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:qualifies ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0038> ;
    rdfs:comment "\"Will be important\" is not a modality the vocabulary has. Left null rather than mapped to the nearest of must/may/should."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-09-02"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0017" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:e910adb71eb7f1d52d06e37ed7b46dc618fcc4f6c6df770466fce554ec158e85" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 188 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The prominence and context of the potentially deceptive or confusing element in the trade mark will be important in deciding whether the trade mark is likely to deceive or cause confusion."@en ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0018>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3/3/1~1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0008> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:statesThresholdFor ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0018" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:20e9513b402bf082b2df83f8f7f0c9c9631b4ffbb949ecb0422e39cceb3341e8" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 139 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "There must be a real and obvious danger of the buying public being deceived and/or confused by the secondary meaning within the trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0022>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3/3/2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0002> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:constrainsExaminerTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0049> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0022" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:d222f7d371d8e06883804bb5b725e0a62be4d39b890ebdbb2fc9ecfcd28d0d16" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 248 ;
    tmk:spanStart 91 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Each application must be considered as it stands in the current marketplace, not in the marketplace as it was in the past and not as it may be in the future."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0023>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3/3/2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:qualifies ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0049> ;
    rdfs:comment "Two unnumbered instrument references in one sentence, neither citable. See GE-0059 and GE-0060."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0023" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:d222f7d371d8e06883804bb5b725e0a62be4d39b890ebdbb2fc9ecfcd28d0d16" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 425 ;
    tmk:spanStart 249 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A sign regarded as deceptive or confusing under the previous legislation may no longer have the same connotation and a ground for rejection may not apply under the current Act."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0024>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/3/3/4> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0040> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0039> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0024" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:075c40b25607ef6a911a15b27e74937b83afcd489266936a56e4839208f9bb3b" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 216 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "In some cases a connotation giving rise to a section 43 ground for rejection may not be obvious during examination and will only emerge at opposition when the full facts of a case are available to the decision maker."@en ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0032>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/4> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:isOvercomeBy ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0013> ;
    rdfs:comment "Subject and object are the wrong way round if `isOvercomeBy` reads as \"X is overcome by Y\". Left as written so the direction problem is visible on at least one record."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0032" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:86800dcce4d41f73e2792ad626162693402011f3c8ba4135bbf91f045f2a7b2f" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1202 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1000 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A section 43 ground for rejection may be overcome by the applicant agreeing to a condition of registration limiting use of the trade mark to goods containing the substance indicated by the relevant INN."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0034>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/5> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0013> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:isOvercomeBy ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0023> ;
    rdfs:comment "GR-0007 and this record carry the same modality value for two different readings. If that is unacceptable, the vocabulary has to grow — and that is a decision, not a bug report."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0034" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:c4235ae85720f19a20037d7a4f5a41161ef68438cf8e1ea2d8e36b90b621b1bb" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 554 ;
    tmk:spanStart 350 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A section 43 ground for rejection may be overcome by the applicant agreeing to a condition of registration limiting use of the trade mark to goods containing substances belonging to the relevant INN stem."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0035>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/6~1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0023> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:qualifies ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0024> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0035" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:66817de6196f7150720015e718aecdc209059307b7d11869b0767ecd18e8e89a" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 373 ;
    tmk:spanStart 192 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Some INN stems consist of simple two or three letter combinations and their presence in a larger word may not be meaningful and as a result would not lead to deception or confusion."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0036>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/5/5/3> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0022> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:dependsOnExternalSource ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0025> ;
    rdfs:comment "The external dependency is stated in the neighbouring chunk rather than this one. If a relationship's support must come from the chunk that states it, this record needs a different `source_ref`."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0036" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:83e38b4ce2a77498c778b9feaa69c1c51f7e1ce3a0e29964705a130cb54639f1" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 484 ;
    tmk:spanStart 338 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Claims for specific pharmaceutical or veterinary goods in Class 5 may also trigger the provisions of section 43 in relation to INNs and INN stems."@en ;
    tmk:tier 2 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0037>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/6%231~1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0026> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0037" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:ac69f55b0b06f0f288ea66d5dc7029193e5cb434b4c2504d45f9e0a087588318" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 228 ;
    tmk:spanStart 49 ;
    tmk:supportingText "If a trade mark contains a name of a person (or group of people) which is well known in relation to the specified goods or services, the provisions of section 43 may be triggered."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0039>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/6%231~2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0029> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:isOvercomeBy ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0039" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:3016fc2af55085c99f6f508c674df732dbefbd36582932ac716f701313b98e1c" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1876 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1704 ;
    tmk:supportingText "An applicant may overcome a section 43 ground for rejection in relation to a name by providing the well-known person’s written permission to use their name as a trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0040>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/6%231~2> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0028> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:qualifies ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0026> ;
    rdfs:comment "Flagged deliberately: if the relationship model cannot hold \"the more X, the less Y\", a large part of the Manual's reasoning cannot be represented at all. Better to know that now than at Stage 4."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0040" ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:3016fc2af55085c99f6f508c674df732dbefbd36582932ac716f701313b98e1c" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 455 ;
    tmk:spanStart 244 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The more common the name, whether it is a given name, surname, or combination of both, the less likely consumers will be to make this assumption, as many well-known people have names shared by many other people."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0042>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/6/6/1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:doesNotGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0030> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0042" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Should ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:94219eaa9c113dcecb64f0c0d8b7d7970ee0c89b4e732ebf371d1b1b4f2abcf1" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 728 ;
    tmk:spanStart 614 ;
    tmk:supportingText "A section 43 ground for rejection should not be raised merely because a trade mark contains the image of a person."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0044>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/6/6/2~1> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0027> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0044" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:May ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:8e7a69fc516a2b4b11213363298946680a0c24f0d1bcddc9f0d803c24c151e53" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 949 ;
    tmk:spanStart 704 ;
    tmk:supportingText "However, a relevant connotation may arise if the deceased person’s estate (or other authorised entity) has continued to control the use of the person’s name/image after their death, e.g. by commercialising directly or licensing to third parties."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0046>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/7%231> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0031> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:constrainsExaminerTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0052> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0046" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Should ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:61ba688909678ff820013ed093969ede20b94f2231822735f4c59fc06b0d38cb" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1448 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1161 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Other phone numbers which do not appear to represent a phoneword should not be queried or researched specifically in respect of section 43, unless other information before the examiner gives them particular reason to suspect that the applicant may not be the licensed user of the number."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0048>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/8/8/3> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0034> ;
    rdfs:comment "The sentence reads \"which could viewed as\" — a missing word in the source. Copied exactly; a corrected supporting text does not land on the passage and the record fails."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0048" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:65247b2f3e686037e599b398b4f74f74a7e40836d32f3e2761a6a12ade582ed8" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 1659 ;
    tmk:spanStart 1405 ;
    tmk:supportingText "Examiners will also need to consider raising a section 41 ground for rejection in relation to any trade mark which could viewed as a radio call sign or frequency that simply consists of that material or with other descriptive or non distinctive elements."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0052>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/9/9/4> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0012> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:extendsTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0017> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0052" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:b338dd460c75842d9658f27fd99008fdf4da4df0d87c90928e6f3157d4509c62" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 173 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The same considerations apply to services as to goods, though careful consideration needs to be given to circumstances which may mitigate the risk of deception or confusion."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0054>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/9/9/5> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:requiresElement ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0013> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0054" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:f62b4939d149235abeefb52354519f2d89394eeed2e2bc8257b6ca5d9d6532c9" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 462 ;
    tmk:spanStart 349 ;
    tmk:supportingText "The condition of registration or specification amendment must directly address the connotation in the trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0056>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/9/9/7> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0050> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:excludesBasis ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0001> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0056" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Must ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:4a152ff8e285012f7bc44941664602f7d5ebbe7775f61faa73472e1827a6bc60" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 649 ;
    tmk:spanStart 436 ;
    tmk:supportingText "When faced with this type of reference it is important to remember that the connotation must be from the trade mark itself and not from any other external considerations such as a reputation in another trade mark."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0057>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/10%231> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:mayGiveRiseTo ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0037> ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0057" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Should ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:7790025faf8751ea416943459edd4d4cc890374c4fc86f400a1ff604c9dd376e" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 266 ;
    tmk:spanStart 0 ;
    tmk:supportingText "If a trade mark, or some part of the trade mark, contains a reference to Indigenous people and a connotation arises from the mark that would be likely to deceive or confuse consumers within the relevant market, then a ground for rejection under s43 should be raised."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GR-0058>
    a tmk:Assertion ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part29/11%231> ;
    rdf:object <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0006> ;
    rdf:predicate tmk:dependsOnExternalSource ;
    rdf:subject <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/concept/GC-0018> ;
    rdfs:comment "Note \"s 43\" with a space here, against \"s43\" in TMM/Part29/10#1 and \"section 43\" elsewhere. Three spellings, one provision, one Part."@en ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-25"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GR-0058" ;
    tmk:hasModality tmk:Should ;
    tmk:sourceContentHash "sha256:4c484f11bb81ae9e0b8453152cd0145a12d14fa09ab434e1c68288097f23886a" ;
    tmk:spanEnd 696 ;
    tmk:spanStart 384 ;
    tmk:supportingText "If during examination of a new application research reveals that a trade mark is identical or similar to a listed EU GI, consideration should then be given to whether or not the use of the trade mark would potentially deceive or confuse Australian consumers and make grounds for rejection under s 43 appropriate."@en ;
    tmk:tier 3 .

